cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A303639 Counterexample Project"
type: software
version: 1.0.1
authors:
  - family-names: "Jeong"
    given-names: "Sunsu"
date-released: 2026-08-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DCLXAI/a303639-counterexample"
abstract: >
  A counterexample (n = 800,322,180) to a 2018 conjecture of Zhi-Wei Sun
  recorded in OEIS A303639, with machine-checkable certificates for all
  136 relevant pairs, an independent verifier, and an obstruction-structure
  analysis explaining why the counterexample occurs and is likely unique.
  Version 1.0.1 corrects the searcher's pair cutoff (152 shifts, not 136, for
  the full 2e9 scan), recomputes the heuristic statistics, bounds the range of
  Lemma 4.1, and replaces Miller-Rabin with unconditional trial division.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - OEIS
  - counterexample
  - computational mathematics
  - sum of two squares
